<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Alpha Biomes: wild animal spawns for eight of its biomes, from Mythic Ages: Megafauna Bestiary (MA_*, 33 entries, gated on
		veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary) and Dark Ages: Beasts and Monsters (DA_*, 13 entries, gated on Van.Beasts).
		This folder only loads with Alpha Biomes (see loadFolders.xml). Each entry carries its own MayRequire, so with neither
		animal mod active these adds contribute nothing. Each biome's add is its own top-level operation, so a biome that goes
		missing in a future Alpha Biomes update cannot stop the others from applying.
		The "vanilla sum" comments are the original author's notes on each biome's existing total commonality.
		From Too Many Mods' AlphaBiomes.xml, where it had no setting.

		Audited 2026-10-13 (analysis/regrowth_audit.py): all 46 pawn kinds exist, none is already in its biome's own list or lists
		the biome in its race's wildBiomes, and no installed mod patches any of them in. That matters: a biome that gets the
		same animal twice throws when it builds its commonality table (BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal), which breaks wild
		animal spawning there.
		Other mods known to add Mythic Ages animals to Alpha Biomes, neither installed here: "Mythic Ages - Alpha Biomes
		Compatibility" (workshop 3779735876, since hidden on Steam) and Joe's Tweaks. Any pair they share with this file would
		be such a duplicate, so they should not be run together with it.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_IdyllicMeadows"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
		<value>
			<!-- vanilla sum: around 9 -->
			<MA_Deermoss MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.02</MA_Deermoss>
		</value>
	</Operation>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="AB_FeraliskInfestedJungle"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
		<value>
			<!-- vanilla sum: 1.11 -->
			<MA_Furpotamus MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Furpotamus>
		</value>
	</Operation>

